      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T19:37:13Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(pathkernel): the crate skeleton, the stage types and the planner switch\n\nAdd the crate camcraft-pathkernel (crates/pathkernel, geometry only;\nmotion depends on it and re-exports it). It holds the stage types of the\nrecord docs/decisions/4024-path-kernel-design.md - recipe, work plane,\ntool shape, verdict, region, guide, order, load, link, entry and exit,\nplan steps - each with checked constructors, unit tests and the stage\ntraits. No planner logic.\n\nAdd the one switch: CAMCRAFT_PLANNER, read one time in\napp::operation::planner_switch and applied in run_job before the arms.\nThe default is the old planner. \"new\" refuses each of the 16 phase-1\nkinds by name.\n\nGate: the crate is in ALL_CRATES, BATCH_CRATES and CLIPPY; a new xtask\ntest checks these lists against the workspace members. AGENTS.md -p list.\n\nRefs #4055\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
