      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T07:33:50Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(pathkernel): make each stage type valid by construction\n\nReview of PR #4123, findings 1 to 6, one rule for each class:\n- valid by construction: private fields, checked constructors, and\n  validated newtypes in each enum variant (WorkPlane, ToolShape, Hop,\n  GuideChoice, LoadControl, Proof, Verdict::Incomplete);\n- order: a curve may only be restarted (closed) or reversed, with its\n  circle; the start is the first point of the first curve;\n- plan: the step law is a transition table; a cut consumes readiness;\n- entry: each proof names its place; the descent stays in it;\n- load: the limit domain, valid records, each reading over the limit\n  named once, each record agrees with a reading;\n- guide: a total order of the set, with a geometric tie-break.\n\nThe tests use the public API in the new suite tests/laws.rs.\n\nRefs #4055\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
